{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Places and People"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": " Is There a Dictionary?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "Beginner"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pencil "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an object we use for writing or drawing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Can I use your pencil? I  want  to write a note. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn1le03ob05aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you hear in a classroom."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "eraser "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a small object we use to remove pencil marks"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:    Do you have an eraser? I need to change something."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn1le03ob05aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dictionary"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a book that has the meaning of words in a language "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Can I use your dictionary? I don't know how to spell a word.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn1le03ob05aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ruler"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a classroom object we use to measure and draw lines"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I need a ruler to draw something. Do you have one?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn1le03ob05aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "desk "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a table we use to  write or work "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are three pencils on the desk.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn1le03ob05aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "big"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "large in size "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My desk is big. I have all my pencils and my dictionary on it!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn1le03ob05aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "small"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "limited in size"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My desk is small. I have no space for writing!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn1le03ob05aud07"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Asking and Saying Where Things Are"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">there is</span> or <span class=\"strong\">there are</span> to say that something is in a specific place. <br /> You use <span class=\"strong\">is there</span> or <span class=\"strong\">are there</span> to ask about something. <br />You use <span class=\"strong\">where is</span> or <span class=\"strong\">where are</span> to ask where something is."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":\"4\",\"columns\":\"3\",\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Singular\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Plural\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Statements with <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> There</ span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"There is <br/>There's  <br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Example: There's a pencil on the desk.</ span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"There are <br/> <br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Example: There are many pencils on the desk.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Questions with <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> There</ span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Is there \u2026 ? <br/><br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Example: Is there a pencil on the desk?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Are there \u2026 ? <br/><br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Example: Are there any pencils on the desk?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Questions with <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Where</ span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Where is \u2026 ? <br/>Where's \u2026 ? <br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Example: Where's the pencil?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Where are \u2026 ?  <br/><br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">Example: Where are the pencils?</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Describing Objects"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\"> adjectives</span> to describe objects. <br />You put adjectives before the noun or after the verb <span class=\"strong\"> to be</span>. <br/> These are the most common types of adjectives: color, size, quality and age."}, {"type": "example", "content": "There is a <span class=\"strong\">red</span> pencil on the desk. (before the noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The pencil is <span class=\"strong\">small</span>. (after the verb)"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":\"05\",\"columns\":\"02\",\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Types of Adjectives</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Examples </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"color\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> red, blue, green, yellow </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"size\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> big, small, short, long</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"quality\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">good, bad, nice </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"age\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> old, new</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "There are <span class=\"strong\">good</span> books in the classroom. (before the noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The books are <span class=\"strong\">new</span>. (after the verb)"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Use information about locations of things to interact with others."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands basic information in English texts according to the communicative topics of this level."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands basic information in English texts according to the communicative topics of this level."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Uses an appropriate range of basic vocabulary and structures to describe location of classroom objects. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands basic information in English texts according to the communicative topics of this level."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Uses an appropriate range of basic vocabulary and structures to describe location of classroom objects. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Uses an appropriate range of basic vocabulary and structures to describe location of classroom objects. "}, {